# Bump babel-monitor revision on every change and build

Whenever you change anything under `contrib/babel-monitor/` that affects the built package or its documented version (source, library, `build.sh`, install docs that embed the APK name, etc.), **increment the package version in the same change set**.

Whenever you run `contrib/babel-monitor/build.sh` (or otherwise produce a new APK), **bump the version first** if it has not already been bumped for this content change. Never rebuild and ship the same `-v` / `packageVersion()` that was already built or installed for different content.

## What to bump

1. In `contrib/babel-monitor/build.sh`, increment the patch segment of `-v` (e.g. `0.1.0` → `0.1.1`).
2. Leave `-r r0` unless the user explicitly asks to bump only the APK release field.
3. Update `packageVersion()` in `contrib/babel-monitor/src/usr/share/ucode/babel_monitor/common.uc` to match (`0.1.N-r0`).
4. Update every APK filename / version string in `contrib/babel-monitor/README.md` (and any other docs touched in that change) to match the new `-v` value.

## When

- Do this for **every** substantive package edit in the same turn as the edit — do not wait to be asked.
- Do this **before every build** that produces an APK for testing, install, or deploy.
- Skip only for changes that cannot affect a build or published version (e.g. this Cursor rule alone, `.gitignore` for local helpers).
- If several edits land in one session before a build/commit, bump **once** per logical change set.
- Do not reuse a version that was already built/installed/pushed for a different content change.
